# 2. Strengthen the HashMap experiment before compiler changes

The current HashMap tests do not strongly exercise actual linear-probing collisions.

For capacity 8 under the experiment's current hash:

```text
1
9
17
```

share the same initial bucket.

Add explicit collision tests.

## Collision chain

Test approximately:

```moss
hm = hash_map(8)

hm.put(1, 10)
hm.put(9, 90)
hm.put(17, 170)

assertEqual(hm.get(1, -1), 10)
assertEqual(hm.get(9, -1), 90)
assertEqual(hm.get(17, -1), 170)
```

## Lookup across tombstone

Test:

```moss
hm.put(1, 10)
hm.put(9, 90)
hm.put(17, 170)

hm.remove(1)

assertEqual(hm.get(9, -1), 90)
assertEqual(hm.get(17, -1), 170)
```

This is the real tombstone-search case.

## Existing key behind tombstone

Important regression:

```moss
hm.put(1, 10)
hm.put(9, 90)

hm.remove(1)

hm.put(9, 900)

assertEqual(hm.size(), 1)
assertEqual(hm.get(9, -1), 900)
```

The insertion algorithm must continue probing after the tombstone before deciding to reuse it, otherwise it could duplicate key `9`.

## Negative collision

Because the current hash normalizes negative keys, also test a pair such as:

```text
5
-5
```

if they share the same initial bucket under the current algorithm.

Do not rely on iteration order in any test.

Keep these experiment tests even after compiler repairs.

