# 7. Reject unsupported local type annotation syntax clearly

Do **not** silently interpret:

```moss
var values: Vector[Int] = []
```

as a binding whose name is:

```text
values: Vector[Int]
```

If local annotations remain unsupported, reject them at parse/check time.

Use a focused structured diagnostic, e.g.:

```text
LOCAL_TYPE_ANNOTATION_UNSUPPORTED
```

Message approximately:

```text
local type annotations are not supported in this form
```

With useful alternatives:

```text
use inferred local syntax: var values = expression
for an empty typed Vector use: var values = Vector[Int]()
```

Likewise reject:

```moss
let x: Int = 3
```

cleanly if local annotations are not part of v0.1.

Do not accidentally introduce general local annotation semantics in this task.

